WEBVTT

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.520
Kei,

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.900
I told you not to come here.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:20.820
Gripen...

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.130
I told you that you wouldn't 
be able to go back.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.880
What can I do?

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.510
I can't choose my dreams.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.460
Tell me...

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.750
In that game, why did you make 
the humans leave the cities?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.180
The optimal answer.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:42.930
The point where the goals of the Xi and 
the win conditions of the game overlap.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.180
Their goal is to wipe us out, right?

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:47.930
No.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.320
Their driving principal is not 
the elimination of humanity.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.930
What are you talking about, Gripen?

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.210
A discrepancy between means and ends.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.450
The obstacle to the ends was,
by chance, humanity.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.760
Wait... What do you mean?

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.250
Essentially...

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.010
What?

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:10.720
I can't hear you...

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.020
Gripen?

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.300
Kei...

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.620
You will have to choose.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.230
Choose... Choose what?

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:36.440
I will ensure you survive until 
all the pieces are in place.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.680
That is my task.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.950
No matter how many times, 
how many dozens of times,

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.940
how many hundreds of times...

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.970
<i>August 9th, 8:00 PM</i>

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.100
Minghua, I'm going for a run.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:32.730
<i>The Mission to Retake Shanghai</i>

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.830
See you later.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.740
<i>What do I tell Minghua?</i>

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.560
<i>I'm joining the operation 
to retake Shanghai.</i>

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.000
<i>We're going right into the enemy's territory.</i>

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.900
<i>It'll be more dangerous than 
anything we've done before.</i>

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:50.740
<i>I might die.</i>

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.190
<i>But this is my chance.</i>

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.720
<i>I can avenge my mom with my own hands,</i>

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.710
<i>and retake my second home.</i>

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.750
<i>If I don't go, I know I'll regret it.</i>

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:09.350
But if I die...

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.720
She'll...

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.190
<b>from: Yashirodoori (SDF)

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:17.330
Should I just go straight to the base?

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.030
Minghua, I need to talk to you 
about something important.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.910
I'm leaving tomorrow.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.080
Where are you going?

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:32.170
I'm going... to take back Shanghai!

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:34.570
Okay, take care!

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:38.510
Welp, I'm just going to ride in a 
fighter jet and shoot down all the Xi!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.960
Bring me back some Hangzhou tea!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.040
Sure thing!

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.440
Yeah, that's not happening.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:46.870
I guess I'll run some more.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.160
Wait!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.330
That's a terrible way to treat a lady.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.640
Phantom!

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:29.550
Sheesh... What if I broke a nail?

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.460
Look at my coat. It's a mess.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:34.620
No, wait... You just tried to kill me!

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.470
I did not. How rude.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.630
I simply hoped you'd be injured badly enough

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:44.830
that you couldn't participate 
in the Shanghai operation.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:50.660
Without you, Gripen will be 
unable to go, of course.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.370
Why do you want fewer people on your side?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:58.080
I believe this operation is sure to fail.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:02.540
Furthermore, I believe it was 
intended to fail from the start.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.390
From the start?

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:06.930
What are you talking about?

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:09.820
They've got a whole fleet 
participating in this!

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.850
And there are four Anima, 
between the US and Japan.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.750
I can't believe they intend 
to lose them all.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:19.240
They have those fakes to 
take our place, don't they?

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.910
This operation will give them real combat 
data to feed back into the drone's systems,

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.290
which can then be mass produced.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:27.080
The Brawlers...

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.260
Unmanned units based on Anima combat data.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:36.210
They've been tested enough, and now all 
that's missing is real combat data.

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:39.260
And they're going to sacrifice us to get it?

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:44.500
The US military doesn't like the fact 
that Japan has more Anima than it does.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.780
So they intend to use this opportunity 
to reduce the number of Japan's Anima,

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.880
and maintain the power balance.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.380
That's how their country thinks.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.140
Does Yashirodoori-san...

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.430
I'm sure he's aware on some level.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.100
But either way...

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:06.680
With no one to protect us,
we'll have to protect ourselves.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:09.950
And I'll do whatever it takes.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:11.570
I see...

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.830
But does that really mean pushing 
me in front of a truck?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.180
If you'd just told me first...

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:20.490
You would've happily jumped out in the road?

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:27.590
You have a reason to risk your life.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.440
You hate the Xi for killing your mother.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:33.800
You'll accept a certain 
degree of risk, won't you?

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.930
Well, I'll let you make the choice.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.110
I believe in you, Kei-san.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:47.270
I'm sure you'll make the smart decision.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:55.090
Minghua...

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:57.650
I know it's too late for this,
but I'm really sorry.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:01.230
I know I've been really terrible to you.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:04.870
I can understand why you 
wouldn't want to talk to me.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:08.790
But there's something I need to tell you.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.840
You're...

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:15.170
the most important person in the world to me.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.660
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.600
Th-The most important person in...

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:25.020
the world?

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.900
Are you serious?

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:31.330
What? Of course I am.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:34.530
I've known you longer than 
anybody else in my life.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:37.700
You've done so much for me
ever since I was little.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:41.950
I owe you more than I owe 
anybody in the world.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:44.020
And?

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:45.240
And?

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.670
Is that all?

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.410
I'm just saying, I'm really grateful to you!

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:53.310
Kei...

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.300
One slap!

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.800
Why?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:03.070
So why did you come tell me this?

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:09.430
I've been thinking so much about 
what I could do to repay you.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.770
You're so nice.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:15.690
You helped me without expecting 
anything in return.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:17.820
But that just wouldn't be right.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.440
I have to be strong, too.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.250
Strong enough to protect you!

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:27.670
And why are you telling me this now?

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:33.060
Um... I'm going to be sleeping over 
at my job tomorrow again, so...

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.220
You're lying, aren't you?

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:36.260
None of this makes sense.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:39.290
Night shifts at work, people from 
the base coming to pick you up...

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:43.840
But you didn't seem like 
you were going to tell me.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:45.850
Minghua...

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.300
Is it dangerous?

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.050
Something to do with everyone's future?

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.660
Something that will help other people?

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.150
Yeah.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.500
And I can't help you?

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:07.210
I'm sorry.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.300
I see!

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:16.130
I was going to try and carry 
all your burdens for you.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:18.260
I'm not sure where things changed.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.630
Nothing's changed.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:23.430
You're strong, and kind, 
and I can respect you.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.790
But right now, there's something only I can do.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:27.970
Okay!

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:30.480
I'll be waiting, then,

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:32.940
for you to finish your job and come home!

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.060
Màn zou!

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:37.840
Wo zou le.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.500
Hey, when do we get there?

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.990
<i>August 10th, 6:00 AM</i>

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.160
I'm bored!

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.080
Let's do something fun till we get there!

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:48.090
She's going nuts...

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.200
Like karaoke or something!

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:50.210
And she's sleeping.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.820
We don't have a mic!

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:54.610
It appears that you ignored my warning.

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:58.150
You think my advice isn't worth heeding?

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:01.940
No, I just decided to accept a necessary risk

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:04.480
for what I want to accomplish.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:10.990
Did you know that the survival 
rate for Roman gladiators was 5%?

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:15.730
But still they fought, dreaming of the 
day they could escape from slavery.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:20.110
I hope that you're not following the 
same line of thought that they did.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:23.760
Then why are you here?

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.530
You don't fight battles 
you can't win, right?

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:30.260
I have far more experience 
than the rest of you.

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:34.580
You seem to have forgotten, 
but Gripen and I beat you.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.450
Whatever.

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:38.290
Hey, we can see it from here!

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.240
Wow!

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:46.740
The ship you see there will be 
our home for this operation.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:48.600
The world's largest warship,

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:52.490
the CVN-78, a.k.a. the USS <i>Gerald R. Ford</i>!

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:59.660
Wow, it's so big! It's huge!

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:01.870
Look at that!

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:04.170
Oh, there you are!

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:06.050
The two-man cell, and...

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:08.410
Two more Anima!

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.720
Wow!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.700
Hello! I'm Rhino!

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:16.920
Good to see you.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.480
Yeah, good to see you again.

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:21.670
Um...

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:22.980
This is Eagle.

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:24.370
And this Phantom.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:27.350
Gripen you've already met.

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:29.020
Nice to meet you.

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:35.260
I've heard you're a terribly loud fighter, 
and I guess what I heard was right.

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.600
When they switched the engine for the model E,

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:40.740
they really forced up the exhaust velocity.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.600
I'm glad to know that a 
veteran like you knows me.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:46.030
And you must be Eagle!

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:49.230
I'm the strongest one here!

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:50.500
I know!

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:54.820
The F-15's kill ratio is 117 to 0, right?

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:57.100
You really are the ultimate fighter!

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.480
I respect you so much!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.820
Y-Yeah?

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.840
She's pretty sociable.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.340
<i>Humans are weird, huh?</i>

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:13.080
We look like humans. 
Will the same thing ever happen to us?

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:14.780
Will we make groups,

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:16.930
draw distinctions between
 friends and outsiders,

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:20.030
and look for things to fight each other over?

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.650
I don't think she's as simple 
a character as she seems.

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:29.370
I think you know more about Anima than I do.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.500
I just don't let my guard down, that's all.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.870
Come inside. I'll explain what we do now.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.070
Willy's waiting.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:41.990
Thanks for coming.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:46.260
I wanted to talk to you before 
the military folks got here.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.270
We're a special unit to begin with.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.680
First, I'll explain the operation.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:58.010
Our goal is to secure a 
beachhead around Shanghai,

00:13:58.010 --> 00:14:01.350
which we can use as a base to launch 
an invasion of the continent.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.610
The first step toward this is 
establishing air superiority.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:07.090
Then we'll launch a bombardment 
of cruise missiles from the fleet,

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:09.150
followed by an amphibious landing.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:12.040
The operation will proceed 
in these three stages.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:15.140
We're taking off from a carrier?

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:18.440
You're just being thrown out 
of a catapult, that's all.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:23.140
If you're that proud of beating me, 
then don't let something like this scare you.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.290
Talk about holding a grudge.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:29.190
The air superiority operation 
will be done with three units.

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:31.960
The first will be standard 
carrier-based crafts.

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:33.690
Their job is to force the 
Xi to divert their forces.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:36.080
Group 2 is the brawlers.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:39.390
They will engage the enemy in the primary 
attack area and reduce their numbers.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:42.300
And the last group is you.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.250
Your job is to achieve air superiority.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.530
So we stay until the very end?

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:51.030
No, once you've used up all your weapons,
 you'll return to Naha.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:52.970
The mission will be complete then.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:59.010
But won't it be dangerous if four Anima 
leave the battlespace at once?

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:03.020
We're going to be fighting 
more Xi than ever, right?

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.990
I understand your concern.

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:06.830
But don't worry.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:09.380
We have our reasons for this.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:14.420
I'll make it simple: there's no 
need to wipe out every last Xi.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:16.530
According to our analysis,

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:20.440
when the Xi lose a certain amount of 
planes in a certain amount of time,

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:23.020
they'll retreat.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.600
We don't know why, but that's 
how their algorithm works.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.860
We'll be taking advantage of that here.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:33.030
Immediately after making contact with the Xi,
we'll bring every unit we have into battle,

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:38.570
reaching that number as quickly as possible
and forcing the retreat algorithm to activate.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:42.780
You're saying that if we start by dealing 
a huge blow, the enemy will retreat?

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:44.390
Theoretically.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:46.910
That's the plan.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.330
Questions?

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:53.010
Does America really intend to win?

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:57.200
I can't speak for the military,

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.320
but I do not intend to lose.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:01.980
I want to know more about the Xi.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:06.670
I want to get close to them, to touch them,
 to inspect them in every way I can,

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:09.250
until I learn their deepest secrets!

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.670
You can tell he was the 
director's classmate.

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:18.910
When you're too smart, 
it screws up your personality.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:22.180
Is that what they call a 
mad scientist, you think?

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:23.630
I'm not sure.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:28.250
Gripen?

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.280
What's wrong?

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:30.620
I'm fine.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:32.680
Just sleepy.

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:35.890
I feel like I'm dreaming, somehow.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:37.970
Dreaming?

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.010
We're here!

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.310
<b>Welcome</b>

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:47.770
<b>Welcome to the CVN-78, Independent Mixed Test Unit</b>

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.730
<b>Welcome to the CVN-78, Independent Mixed Test Unit</b>

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:49.740
Welcome!

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:58.950
I'll introduce you, everybody!

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.590
This is the captain!

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:01.650
Seriously?

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:04.660
At ease.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:10.080
We're proud to get a chance to go 
on a mission with Japan's Anima.

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:13.970
Please, enjoy the party.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:26.730
Having fun?

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.070
Bring me more awamori!

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.670
Don't drink too much!

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.830
Humans are illogical.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:44.010
See how differently the organization 
and its members view things?

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:46.210
Is that why you can't be friends with us?

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.000
It's not good to get too attached, is it?

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:55.080
If things go south, we'll have to 
abandon them in order to survive.

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:58.040
Don't you get tired of being that way?

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:00.800
Everyone else just takes things too easy.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.480
Whatcha doin'?

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:08.600
You're two of the party's stars.
You can't leave.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.820
I put a lot of effort into planning this.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:11.890
Oh, sorry.

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:13.690
Just kidding.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.730
It's fine if you want to take a break.

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:19.200
We don't want you getting 
sick before the operation.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:23.520
The veteran here probably needs to take 
extra-good care of her health, especially.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:27.250
Is that a way of telling an 
old lady she's not welcome?

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:30.820
I was just thinking that I may have aimed 
the party too much at a younger crowd.

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:34.070
I should've taken into consideration that 
the elderly would be in attendance.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.830
Next!

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:41.710
She's cute.

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:45.680
Hey, Narutani Kei.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:49.810
I know you're all cautious around me.

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:55.810
But I wish that times like 
these could continue forever.

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:58.160
I want you to believe that.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:03.660
Don't you think it would be wonderful if we 
could have another party like this in Shanghai?

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:04.910
Yeah.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.630
Okay, enjoy the party!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:13.530
But will I be there when it happens?

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:19.040
Why are Gripen and I in the same room?

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:21.580
You and I are partners.

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:23.840
Together, we're a single tactical unit.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:26.060
It's natural for us to be in the same room.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:31.130
Normally, you'd put a man and 
a woman in different rooms, right?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.310
W-Wait!

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:39.500
Why are you taking off your clothes?

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:43.370
I'm changing into my sweats.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:48.110
Listen! Do it on your bed, 
and close the curtains first!

00:19:48.110 --> 00:19:48.970
Why?

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:52.500
Because if you don't, I'll cause 
problems for the mission!

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:56.550
I don't understand, but if you say so.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.200
Will this do?

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.330
Yeah.

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:06.790
Hey, how are you feeling now?

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:08.750
Don't worry about me.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.710
Are you all right, Kei?

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:11.550
Me?

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:14.360
The atmosphere around you seemed 
tense even at the party.

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:15.200
It's strange.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.740
What do you mean, the atmosphere around me?

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.260
Are you sure you're not thinking it 
would be okay if you were shot down?

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:33.430
No way.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:36.440
I understand how strongly you feel.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:37.350
But...

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:42.550
If you intend to sacrifice 
your life for the mission,

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.630
I'll go alone.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:47.290
I...

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:49.460
No, you're right.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:52.690
I'll do whatever it takes 
to achieve my goal.

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:54.650
I don't care if I die doing it.

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:58.340
That's how I feel.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:02.460
I don't care about how you feel,

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:05.180
even though the plane isn't mine alone.

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:06.870
I'm sorry.

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:07.930
No...

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:11.170
I'm not that attached to my own life.

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:14.290
And I'm not going to tell you 
that what you want is wrong.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:18.680
I just want you to feel like 
you want to come home alive.

00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:22.220
To complete the mission 
successfully and safely.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:26.960
I want to hear that from you.

00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:28.650
Gripen...

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:35.510
I am your wings.

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:37.150
Your lance.

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:41.650
Give the word, and I will go 
anywhere to defeat your enemies.

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:53.640
Let's go home alive together, Gripen!

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:29.760
Next time on <i>Girly Air Force</i>...

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:33.170
ALT 11: "A Homeland with No One Home."

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>A Homeland with No One Home</i>

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:37.900
Barbie 01, cleared for take off!
